WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're on the
House Intelligence Committee.

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've been dealing a lot with
the Russian investigation.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.605
So, I'm happy you're here, but I
don't think Donald Trump is.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.073 line:92%
He tweeted about you recently.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.043 size:81% position:41%
And right here we see,
"Sleazy Adam Schiff,

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
the totally biased Congressman
looking into Russia,

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
spends all of his time
on television..."

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
so he's got you there.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
"...pushing
the Dem loss excuse."

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.086 line:92%
So, when you first saw that,

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the president
of the United States,

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:22.322 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
how did you feel?

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:25.892
-Well, I was getting on
the plane to fly to Washington,

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my phone
lit up with messages.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The president
just called you a sleaze."

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:30.730 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.266 size:78% position:39%
-And my reaction was,
"I've been slimed."

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:33.700 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like a character
on "Ghostbusters."

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:36.770 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You did.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.570 line:92%
-But my second reaction was,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.739
he really should've talked
to my friends from grade school.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.340 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.343
-With a name like Schiff, they
did much better than he did.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:44.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a lot of material
to work with there.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he usually does
a really good with his, like,

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:48.314 size:81% position:41% line:92%
disparaging nicknames.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I feel like
he dropped the ball.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.784 line:92%
-It was a missed opportunity.

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:52.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like
you're making him so angry

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:55.455
that you're blinding his ability
to really dig in.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.756 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.724 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-This is true.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.593 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.195
-So, I want to talk about
The Wall Street Journal

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:05.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
reported tonight
that Special Counsel Mueller

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.434 line:92%
has opened up a grand jury.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, you have
a different investigation.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.671
You're the House Intelligence
Committee's investigation.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a
Senate Judiciary Committee.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a
Senate Intelligence Committee.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
The grand jury is separate,
but what can --

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:18.344 size:88% position:44% line:92%
What does this tell you,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
as somebody
with your legal background,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he has opened up
a grand jury?

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, his responsibility
is really different

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
than all of ours in Congress,
because we're looking at

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
the whole range
of what Russia did,

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:32.492
their active measures campaign,
what tactics they employed.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:35.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's looking
at a very specific task,

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that is,
were U.S. laws violated,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if so,
who should be prosecuted?

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:42.902
And the fact that he has now
apparently, or reportedly,

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.271 size:75% position:38%
gone to a grand jury
means he now needs

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
the power of compulsion
to get documents

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.776 line:92%
to compel witnesses to testify.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.845 size:88% position:44% line:92%
That is a necessary step

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:54.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
to move forward
to a potential prosecution.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
Doesn't mean
that he will prosecute.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:00.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this is
part of an investigation

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:00.854 line:92%
very much moving forward.

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:04.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And another report said
that he's sort of moving into

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.659 line:92%
the financial element of this.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.194 line:92%
Donald Trump had said recently,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
in speaking about
Special Counsel Mueller,

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.664 size:78% position:39%
that that was sort of
a red line for him.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why do you think it is
that Donald Trump

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
is so worried about
the financial part

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:17.937 size:81% position:41% line:92%
of this investigation?

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.240
-Well, I'll tell you why
I'm so concerned about it,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that is, when people think
about kompromat,

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:25.545 size:88% position:44%
what the Russians call
"compromising material,"

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:28.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
they tend to think about
the dossier,

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.750 line:92%
potentially salacious videos.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.152 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-It's all I think about.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.622 line:92%
I wish you hadn't brought it up.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The far more compromising
material would be

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.194 line:92%
if the Russians were engaged,

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
as they do in other places,
like Europe,

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
in illicit
financial transactions

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.333 size:81% position:41%
and money laundering
or something like that

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.201 line:92%
with the Trump organization.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then, they would have very
powerful compromising material

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:54.407
they could hold over his head,
and it could affect U.S. policy.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:58.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
So if Bob Mueller
is looking into this,

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
it's really quite necessary

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:03.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make sure
that our policy is based

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:04.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
on U.S.
national security interests,

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:09.055
not the personal exposure of the
president of the United States.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, obviously, this deeply
worries the president.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:12.959 line:92%
Now, whether that says something

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:16.296
about his financial dealings
in the past remains to be seen,

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
but plainly,
this is what got him,

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:22.001
once again, to talk about
possibly removing Mueller.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:25.271
-Now, you were talking about,
"Did the Russians do anything

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:28.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
to compromise
the Trump administration,

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:28.841 line:92%
Donald Trump personally?"

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is interesting,
because the Russians,

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
you could find
in your investigation

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the Russians did things,
and it turns out

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the Trumps
were not aware of this.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Jared Kushner
sort of made that argument --

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:40.553
it was in a leaked audio --
to Congressional interns

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we couldn't have
colluded with the Russians.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
He basically said,
"We couldn't even collude

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:45.725 size:84% position:42% line:92%
with our own campaign."

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:50.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, basically, making
an argument of incompetence.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.999 line:92%
Which isn't a bad argument.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:53.566 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:56.970
-Well, and the speaker has often
made the same argument.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:57.403 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, "Don't hold
the president responsible.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
He doesn't know
what he's doing."

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:01.541 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-"He's new."

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"He's new."
-Yeah.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.744 size:84% position:42%
-"He's inexperienced.
He's not a politician."

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All things that would've
been great to hear

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.680 line:92%
on the campaign trail, yeah.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.816 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. Absolutely.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.718 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:14.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I want to ask this,
as well.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.923
I'm imagining that you have
a lot of people that see you

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:20.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
and see your investigation
as some sort of savior

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.194 line:92%
for the Democratic party.

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, this, you're gonna
discover something

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's gonna
push him out of office.

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:28.968
It strikes me that the Democrats
are at risk right now,

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a party,
of putting too much stock

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:34.274 line:92%
in hoping that an investigation

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
brings about the end
of the Trump administration

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:39.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the focus should be
at where you hope

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
administrations end --
at the ballot box.

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:44.384
Do you think the Democratic
party is doing enough messaging

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:48.321
outside of their investigations
into the Trump administration,

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as,
"Hey, the next time you vote,

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:53.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
we actually have a message
that is independent

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:57.363
of what we think is wrong with
the current people in power"?

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, this is, I think,
absolutely essential,

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:02.368
and that is, yes, we have do go
forward with the investigation,

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:05.204
and that's very important
for the reasons we talked about,

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:08.408
but more than that, we need
to give voters a positive --

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:11.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
a powerful positive reason
to vote for Democrats,

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just all the reasons
they don't like Donald Trump,

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:15.748 size:88% position:44% line:92%
which they know already.

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think
the real key to that

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.453
is addressing the economic
concerns that people have,

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:22.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
particularly
in distressed communities

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they look
at a small global world.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:26.726 size:88% position:44%
They look at automation
replacing a lot of jobs,

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:29.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they ask, and they have
every right to ask,

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What are you offering us
to give us hope

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:33.333 line:92%
that our lives can be better,

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
that our children's lives
can be better?"

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have every right
to ask that.

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need to have
a good answer for them.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Republicans
have no answer except,

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:42.408 line:92%
"You're gonna win so much,

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're gonna be
tired of winning."

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, they're
not tired of winning.

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:48.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But we owe them
a good answer, too,

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:49.682 line:92%
and we are working on it.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:53.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's, I think, not only vital
to the Democratic party,

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:54.454 line:92%
it's vital to the country.

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
If we're gonna have
a situation where we continue

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
to pass on
to the next generation

00:05:59.058 --> 00:05:59.759 line:92%
a higher quality of life,

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:02.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're gonna have to answer
that very difficult

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
but very important
economic question.

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:07.066
-I look forward to seeing --
hearing what those answers are

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.000 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
from the party.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.869 line:92%
Last thing -- every day --

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:11.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
I pay attention to this stuff
every day.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
The part of me
that can be shocked --

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:14.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
I keep waiting to be numbed --
but every day,

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:17.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
something happens
where I go, "What?!"

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.145 line:92%
Does that still happen for you?

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:21.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Every day it happens.
-Okay.

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It --
-All right.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's nice to see
you're not jaded.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:28.988
-I like to say I'm running out
of adjectives and expletives.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, there you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:31.457 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We have to start --

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.626 size:84% position:42%
Yeah, we have to find
more of those for this.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:36.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
Really appreciate it.
-Thank you.

00:06:36.763 --> 00:06:39.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congressman Adam Schiff,
everybody!

